			<div class="content" id="post-content-4642840">
									

<p>Any article should be able to survive on its own merits and rely on reading an entirely new piece to enjoy. It's true that some articles are improved by reading them as an over-arching story, but crosslinks are meant to <em>enhance</em> the story, they shouldn't <em>be</em> the story.</p>
<p>As for the article itself, I find myself sharing similar sentiments to Flops. I actually have read the other articles before this one, but all-in-all I'm not really seeing too much of a connection besides &quot;demons&quot;.</p>
<p>I will say though that I did quite enjoy the dialogue between the two officers and the parrot, because I always get a kick out of people unfamiliar with the anomalous interacting with it, and I feel you did that quite well here.</p>

